WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.059
The wild animal was silent.

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.602
My family looked down anxiously from our nest in the treetop.

3
00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:07.531
"Come, Fritz," I whispered.

4
00:00:07.532 --> 00:00:11.211
"We must go down and find out what was making that awful noise."

5
00:00:11.212 --> 00:00:14.862
We picked up our guns, and he followed me down the steps.

6
00:00:14.863 --> 00:00:18.206
Outside we glided carefully from tree to tree.

7
00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:22.443
Suddenly we heard that awful sound again, and it was quite nearby!

8
00:00:22.444 --> 00:00:25.669
Fritz raised his gun, but quickly lowered it.

9
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:31.017
"It's only Grizzle." He laughed as our missing donkey appeared before us.

10
00:00:31.018 --> 00:00:32.904
Our friend was not alone.

11
00:00:32.905 --> 00:00:38.503
Behind him trotted another animal resembling a donkey, but slim and graceful as a horse.

12
00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.777
"That's a wild donkey, Fritz," I whispered.

13
00:00:41.778 --> 00:00:45.890
"Creep back to Falconhurst and bring me two pieces of rope."

14
00:00:45.891 --> 00:00:50.157
He soon returned with the rope and some oats.

15
00:00:50.158 --> 00:00:54.080
The wild donkey followed Grizzle's lead and nibbled some oats.

16
00:00:54.081 --> 00:00:57.906
I quickly threw the rope around her neck while Fritz captured Grizzle.

17
00:00:57.907 --> 00:01:02.860
Despite the wild donkey's kicking and struggling, I managed to lead her back to Falconhurst.

18
00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:08.158
We tied both animals under the roots of our tree for the night.

19
00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:14.947
The next morning I realized that we needed to provide better shelter for our animals and ourselves before the rainy season arrived.

20
00:01:14.948 --> 00:01:20.933
In addition to our new donkey—which we named Lightfoot— three broods of chickens had recently hatched.

21
00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:25.236
We began by constructing walls and a roof over the roots of our tree.

22
00:01:25.237 --> 00:01:31.211
After fastening bamboo canes tightly together, we filled any holes with clay and moss.

23
00:01:31.212 --> 00:01:35.789
Then we coated the roof and walls with tar to make everything waterproof.

24
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.566
I divided the space into rooms.

25
00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:46.256
Stables, henhouse, kitchen, and dining room were soon all under one roof.

26
00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:54.157
Every day we loaded our cart with provisions for our winter quarters: cassava, potatoes, coconuts, and other foods.

27
00:01:54.158 --> 00:02:00.307
One day when we were out gathering nuts, Ernest found a nest made from long, broad grass.

28
00:02:00.308 --> 00:02:05.325
"I'll take some of this grass home for Franz," said Ernest, waving a piece around.

29
00:02:05.326 --> 00:02:07.281
"He can pretend it's a sword."

30
00:02:07.282 --> 00:02:11.273
When we arrived home, Franz was delighted with his new toy.

31
00:02:11.274 --> 00:02:13.273
But Mother was even happier.

32
00:02:13.274 --> 00:02:15.880
"That's not grass," she said.

33
00:02:15.881 --> 00:02:21.845
"That's flax. Once it's properly prepared, I can make linen for clothing."

34
00:02:21.846 --> 00:02:25.739
So we added soaking the flax in water to our tasks.

35
00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.798
Soon the rain began to fall, and we had to retreat to our shelter under the roots.

36
00:02:30.799 --> 00:02:36.031
We carried down any furniture or household items that might be damaged by the moisture.

37
00:02:36.032 --> 00:02:40.082
With our beds all around us, our dwelling was crowded indeed.

38
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:44.460
We gradually rearranged our things so that we had more room.

39
00:02:44.461 --> 00:02:48.353
During the day we sent our formerly wild animals outside.

40
00:02:48.354 --> 00:02:51.544
We figured that they were used to surviving the rainy season.

41
00:02:51.545 --> 00:02:55.148
Every night Fritz and I went outside to bring them back in.

42
00:02:55.149 --> 00:02:58.665
And every night we returned home soaked to the skin.

43
00:02:58.666 --> 00:03:04.229
"You need waterproof suits," said my wife. "Let me make some for you."

44
00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.906
First she sewed a hood to a heavy shirt.

45
00:03:06.907 --> 00:03:09.791
Then she attached the shirt to some pants.

46
00:03:09.792 --> 00:03:14.861
She coated the whole outfit with layers of rubber to produce a wonderful waterproof suit.

47
00:03:14.862 --> 00:03:18.597
Time dragged despite our efforts to keep busy.

48
00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:23.096
Our days were occupied with caring for our animals and doing chores.

49
00:03:23.097 --> 00:03:26.978
In the evenings I wrote in my journal while my wife sewed.

50
00:03:26.979 --> 00:03:32.841
Ernest made sketches of the birds, animals, and flowers that he had encountered since our arrival.

51
00:03:32.842 --> 00:03:36.915
Fritz and Jack taught little Franz to read.

52
00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.478
At last the rainy season was over.

53
00:03:39.479 --> 00:03:43.716
We climbed up to our nest and found it filled with broken branches.

54
00:03:43.717 --> 00:03:47.547
"Is Falconhurst ruined?" cried Franz.

55
00:03:47.548 --> 00:03:50.164
"No, no, my boy," I reassured him.

56
00:03:50.165 --> 00:03:53.763
"There's nothing here that a few days of hard work can't fix."

57
00:03:53.764 --> 00:03:57.893
I was more worried about Tentholm.

58
00:03:57.894 --> 00:04:03.148
And sure enough we found that the tent was blown down and the canvas torn to rags.

59
00:04:03.149 --> 00:04:07.730
Our provisions were soaked, and two kegs of gunpowder were ruined.

60
00:04:07.731 --> 00:04:12.655
The sailboat was safe, but the tub boat had been destroyed by the waves.

61
00:04:12.656 --> 00:04:17.089
"We need to find a better place to spend the rainy season," I said to Fritz.

62
00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.180
He looked at the rocky cliffs surrounding Tentholm.

63
00:04:20.181 --> 00:04:22.862
"Maybe we could hollow out a cave in the rock."

64
00:04:22.863 --> 00:04:32.529
A few days later we loaded up our cart with hammers, chisels, pickaxes, and crowbars.

65
00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:37.451
The three older boys and I battered away at the rock without making much progress.

66
00:04:37.452 --> 00:04:42.514
But on the tenth day, Jack suddenly shouted, "I lost my crowbar!

67
00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:46.030
It fell through a hole and I heard it crash down inside!"

68
00:04:46.031 --> 00:04:50.394
We rushed to his side. "There must be a cavern in there," I said.

69
00:04:50.395 --> 00:04:54.311
With a shout of joy, the boys attacked the rock.

70
00:04:54.312 --> 00:05:01.199
And soon the hole was large enough for us to enter the cave.

